===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|säugen|Tier|t1=suck, suckle|t2=animal|lang=de}}. The part ''Säuge-'' ( from {{term|säugen}} "to suckle" ) is part of the compound because the offspring of mammals is fed by their respective parent by breastfeeding them.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈzɔɪ̯ɡəˌtiːɐ̯/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Säugetiers|Säugetiere}}

# [[mammal]]
#: ''Die Ameisenigel und das Schnabeltier sind die einzige '''Säugetiere''', die Eier legen.'' — The spiny anteater and the platypus are the only mammals that lay eggs.

